# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/controls/rfc-tr.md#4-table-content-split-into-rows
# provenance: PV-0910, PV-0912, PV-0913, PV-0914, PV-0919
# kind: rfc-table-content
# description: One row, then the end item followed by its own trailing pair, which is not table content.
# derivation: Row per PV-0910/PV-0913; the reassembler stops after the 03 06 item's length (IMPL-CT-3), so its trailing pair is reported as 2 trailing bytes.
# expect.rows: 1
# expect.row.1.offset: 4
# expect.row.1.length: 10
# expect.content_length: 10
# expect.content: 5A 5A 5F 42 49 53 43 55 49 54
# expect.end_length: 0
# expect.trailing: 2
# expect.error: none
hex:
03 05 00 0A                                       # item 03 05 (table content), length 10
5A 5A 5F 42 49 53 43 55 49 54                     # value of row 1
03 05                                             # trailing id pair 03 05 (PV-0919)
03 06 00 00                                       # item 03 06 (table content end), length 0
03 06                                             # trailing id pair 03 06 (after the table: reported as trailing)
